<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Leo X</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1475">1475</a>–<a href="/years/1521">1521</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Leo X, Giovanni di Lorenzo de' Medici, Leone X · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-medici">House of Medici</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Leo X, born Giovanni di <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorenzo-de-medici">Lorenzo de' Medici</a>, was head of the Catholic Church and leader of the Papal States from 1513 until his death in 1521. The second son of Lorenzo de' Medici of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, he was named a cardinal in 1489 at the age of 13. As pope he oversaw the closing sessions of the Fifth Council of the Lateran and in 1517 waged a costly war to secure his nephew as Duke of Urbino. His granting of indulgences for the rebuilding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-peters-basilica">St. Peter's Basilica</a> was challenged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a>, whom his bull Exsurge Domine condemned in 1520. A great patron of the arts, he saw <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raphael">Raphael</a> decorate the Vatican rooms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-leo-x.jpg" alt="Pope Leo X" width="330" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Bini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raffaello,_ritratto_di_papa_leone_X_tra_i_cardinali_luigi_de'_rossi_e_giulio_de'_medici,_1518,_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Medici it raised gave the Church two popes, <b>Leo X</b> and Clement VII, and later two queens of France.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-florence">Republic of Florence · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>The worldly excesses of the Renaissance Church, epitomised by the era of Alexander VI (1492–1503), intensified under <b>Pope Leo X</b> (1513–1521), whose use of indulgences to raise funds for Saint Peter’s Basilica was a key impetus for Martin Luther’s 95 Theses.</blockquote><a href="/movement/counter-reformation">Counter-Reformation · Background</a></li><li><blockquote>To raise money for the rebuilding of St Peter’s Basilica in Rome, <b>Pope Leo X</b> authorised a campaign of indulgence preaching in the lands of Albert of Brandenburg, archbishop of Mainz and Magdeburg, under an agreement that half the proceeds would repay the loan Albert had taken from…</blockquote><a href="/movement/protestant-reformation">Protestant Reformation · Background</a></li><li><blockquote>Outside Wittenberg's Elster Gate, Martin Luther burned <b>Leo X</b>'s bull threatening him with excommunication, along with books of canon law.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-10">10 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Pope Leo X</b> granted Henry VIII the title Fidei Defensor for his treatise attacking Martin Luther.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-11">11 October in history</a></li><li><blockquote>A surviving son, Giovanni Maria, regained the city, and <b>Pope Leo X</b> made him duke in 1515.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-camerino">Duchy of Camerino</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.77,11.25&amp;year=1504" aria-label="Florence on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4820 613 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Pope Leo X"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5270 883h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5270 883h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.77,11.25&amp;year=1504">What was here in 1504? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
